tyrmel - a terminal that looks like the console and shows pictures
==================================================================
The console's font and colours, and pictures right in the terminal the way
kitty does them, so yazi's previews and anything else that speaks
kitty's graphics protocol just work.

One C file on libvterm, Xft and libpng. Icons come from a Nerd Font if you
have one, letters it hasn't got from whatever font has them.

Install
-------
	make
	sudo make install

Settings
--------
~/.config/tyrmel/config, made the first time it starts:

	font = VGA
	font size = 16
	scrollback = 10000
	cursor = block
	shell =
	background colour = black
	text colour = grey
	cursor colour = grey
	colour 1 = #aa0000

Change a line and save, it works straight away.

Keys
----
	Ctrl+Shift+c        copy
	Ctrl+Shift+v        paste
	Shift+Insert        paste what's selected
	Shift+PageUp/Down   scroll back, or the mouse wheel
	Ctrl+Shift+plus     bigger font, minus smaller, 0 back

Select with the mouse, two clicks for a word, three for the line.
Ctrl+click an address to open it. Hold shift to select in programs that
use the mouse.

It takes xterm's -T, -class, -geometry, -hold and -e, so it can stand in
for xterm. -fs SIZE sets the font size for that one window.
